# Everything a benchmark run produces is regenerated by `python run.py <pair>`
# and must never be committed.  Rather than deny-list the artifact types we
# happen to have seen (.pt, .jsonl, .log, .bin, .npy, .arrow, .pth, ...), this
# is an **allow-list**: ignore everything, then re-include source only.  A new
# kind of output therefore stays ignored by default.

*
!.gitignore
!*/
!*.py
!*.md
!*.yaml
!*.sbatch

# The re-includes above apply at any depth, and generated stores contain their
# own .yaml/.json config (e.g. bergson_index/config.yaml).  Excluding those
# directories outright wins: nothing under an excluded directory can be
# re-included, whatever its extension.
__pycache__/
archive/
slurm/logs/
*/checkpoints/
*/data_cache/
*/*_grads*/
*/*_index*/
*/*_logs/
*/*_store/
*/compact_fisher_probe/
*/_probe_test/
